{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Eloah.</b> Now he will recount how many mighty deeds He did for Israel. The meaning: \"Are you not He from Teman?\" — like \"chief of Teman,\" like \"YHWH, when You came forth from Seir.\"" "<b>And the Holy One from Mount Paran.</b> I have already explained this meaning in the section of Va'zot HaBerakhah, for when the Glory passed over Mount Seir, which is adjacent to Paran — as it is stated: \"and the Horite in their mountain, Seir, as far as El-Paran\" — then the Glory of HaShem shone forth from Seir, and His might was seen in the war against Midian and Sihon and Og." "<b>His glory covered the heavens.</b> That all praised Him and were in dread of Him."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:03.999795898Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}